      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from stdin at once to handle large I/O efficiently\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    \n    if not input_data:\n        return\n\n    iterator = iter(input_data)\n    \n    try:\n        # First token is the number of test cases\n        num_test_cases = int(next(iterator))\n    except StopIteration:\n        return\n        \n    results = []\n    \n    for _ in range(num_test_cases):\n        try:\n            # Read n\n            n = int(next(iterator))\n            \n            # Read the n integers for array weights and build the prefix sum array P\n            # P[i] will store the sum of the first i elements (a[0]...a[i-1])\n            # This allows computing subarray sums in O(1) time\n            P = [0] * (n + 1)\n            current_sum = 0\n            \n            for i in range(n):\n                val = int(next(iterator))\n                current_sum += val\n                P[i+1] = current_sum\n                \n        except StopIteration:\n            break\n            \n        ans = 0\n        # We want to find the maximum absolute difference between weights of two trucks.\n        # For a chosen k (number of boxes per truck), the array is divided into n/k trucks.\n        # If there is only 1 truck (k=n), the difference is 0.\n        # Since we want the maximum difference, we only consider k such that n/k >= 2.\n        # This implies k <= n // 2.\n        \n        limit = n // 2\n        \n        # Iterate over all possible k (number of boxes per truck)\n        for k in range(1, limit + 1):\n            if n % k == 0:\n                # k is a divisor of n. Calculate weights of all trucks.\n                # Truck j (0-indexed) carries boxes from index j*k to (j+1)*k - 1.\n                # The sum of weights for this truck is P[(j+1)*k] - P[j*k].\n                \n                # We generate the list of truck weights.\n                # range(0, n, k) iterates through start indices 0, k, 2k, ..., n-k.\n                truck_weights = [P[i+k] - P[i] for i in range(0, n, k)]\n                \n                # Calculate the difference between the heaviest and lightest truck\n                # Since n/k >= 2, truck_weights has at least 2 elements.\n                current_diff = max(truck_weights) - min(truck_weights)\n                \n                if current_diff > ans:\n                    ans = current_diff\n                    # Optimization: if ans is already large, we don't need to check if we could bound it?\n                    # But without a theoretical upper bound, we must check all.\n        \n        results.append(str(ans))\n        \n    sys.stdout.write('\\n'.join(results) + '\\n')\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    solve()\n```",
