    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Here’s the Python function that solves the problem:  \n\n```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n\n    # Read input\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    A = list(map(int, data[:9]))\n    B = list(map(int, data[9:]))\n\n    # Calculate total runs\n    total_takahashi = sum(A)\n    total_aoki = sum(B)\n\n    # Aoki needs to have strictly more runs than Takahashi after bottom of 9th\n    # Let x be runs scored in bottom of 9th\n    # Then total_aoki + x > total_takahashi\n    # So x > total_takahashi - total_aoki\n    # Since x must be integer, min x = total_takahashi - total_aoki + 1\n    # But if total_takahashi - total_aoki + 1 is negative, they already won? No,\n    # they haven’t played bottom of 9th yet, but constraint says Takahashi total >= Aoki total so diff >= 0\n    diff = total_takahashi - total_aoki\n    answer = diff + 1\n\n    print(answer)\n\nsolve()\n```",
