    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3.5-9b",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom itertools import combinations\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef solve(nums: List[int], k: int) -> int:\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    n = len(nums)\n    nums.sort()\n    \n    total_power = 0\n    \n    for subseq in combinations(n, k):\n        current_min_diff = float('inf')\n        for i in range(k - 1):\n            diff = abs(subseq[i + 1] - subseq[i])\n            if diff < current_min_diff:\n                current_min_diff = diff\n        total_power = (total_power + current_min_diff) % MOD\n    \n    return total_power\n```\n\nWait, the above is incorrect. `combinations(n, k)` selects indices, not values. Let me fix the solution:\n\n```python\nfrom itertools import combinations\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef solve(nums: List[int], k: int) -> int:\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    def get_power(subseq: List[int]) -> int:\n        if k < 2:\n            return 0\n        subseq.sort()\n        min_diff = float('inf')\n        for i in range(k - 1):\n            diff = subseq[i + 1] - subseq[i]\n            min_diff = min(min_diff, diff)\n        return min_diff if min_diff != float('inf') else 0\n    \n    total = 0\n    \n    for sub in combinations(nums, k):\n        power = get_power(list(sub))\n        total = (total + power) % MOD\n    \n    return total\n```",
