      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findMissingAndRepeatedValues(grid):\n    n = len(grid)\n    total_elements = n * n\n    \n    # Flatten the grid and count frequencies\n    flat_grid = []\n    for row in grid:\n        flat_grid.extend(row)\n    \n    # Count frequency of each number\n    freq = {}\n    for num in flat_grid:\n        freq[num] = freq.get(num, 0) + 1\n    \n    # Find the repeated number (appears twice)\n    repeated = None\n    for num, count in freq.items():\n        if count == 2:\n            repeated = num\n            break\n    \n    # Find the missing number\n    missing = None\n    for num in range(1, total_elements + 1):\n        if num not in freq:\n            missing = num\n            break\n    \n    return [repeated, missing]\n```",
