      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_repeating_missing(grid):\n    n = len(grid)\n    N = n * n\n    \n    # Calculate the sum and sum of squares of all elements in the grid\n    actual_sum = sum(x for row in grid for x in row)\n    actual_sq_sum = sum(x * x for row in grid for x in row)\n    \n    # Calculate the sum and sum of squares for numbers 1 to N\n    # Sum of 1 to N: N * (N + 1) / 2\n    expected_sum = N * (N + 1) // 2\n    # Sum of squares 1 to N: N * (N + 1) * (2 * N + 1) / 6\n    expected_sq_sum = N * (N + 1) * (2 * N + 1) // 6\n    \n    # The difference in sums gives (a - b)\n    # Explanation: actual_sum = Sum(all numbers) + a - b\n    #                       expected_sum = Sum(all numbers)\n    # => actual_sum - expected_sum = a - b\n    diff_sum = actual_sum - expected_sum\n    \n    # The difference in sum of squares gives (a^2 - b^2)\n    # Explanation: actual_sq_sum = Sum(x^2) + a^2 - b^2\n    #                       expected_sq_sum = Sum(x^2)\n    # => actual_sq_sum - expected_sq_sum = a^2 - b^2\n    diff_sq_sum = actual_sq_sum - expected_sq_sum\n    \n    # We know (a^2 - b^2) = (a - b)(a + b)\n    # So (a + b) = (a^2 - b^2) / (a - b)\n    sum_ab = diff_sq_sum // diff_sum\n    \n    # Solve the system of linear equations:\n    # 1) a - b = diff_sum\n    # 2) a + b = sum_ab\n    # Adding (1) and (2): 2a = sum_ab + diff_sum  => a = (sum_ab + diff_sum) // 2\n    # Subtracting (1) from (2): 2b = sum_ab - diff_sum => b = (sum_ab - diff_sum) // 2\n    \n    a = (sum_ab + diff_sum) // 2\n    b = (sum_ab - diff_sum) // 2\n    \n    return [a, b]\n```",
