    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_507",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: As a result of a blow-out, Frank Lincoln's car swerved and hit John Martin's car.Leon Taylor, a passenger in Mr. Martin's car, had medical expenses of $6,251. Mr. Martin's medical billscame to $75. If Lincoln had 5/10 bodily injury insurance, howmuch will his insurance company pay?\n\nOptions: \nA. $5,251\nB. $11,000\nC. $6,251\nD. $10,326\nE. $10,000\nF. $6,326\nG. $5,075\nH. $7,500\nI. $6,000\nJ. $5,000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
