    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To minimize the cost, we express the total cost in terms of radius $ r $ and height $ h $, using the volume constraint $ \\pi r^2 h = 10 $. The cost function is $ C = 2(2\\pi r^2) + 1.5(2\\pi rh) $, since the top and bottom cost $2 per sq ft and the side costs $1.50. Minimizing this function subject to the volume constraint leads to $ r \\approx 1.061 $ ft and $ h \\approx 2.828 $ ft.\n\nThis matches option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
