      "generated_answer": "The Durbin-Watson statistic is used to detect autocorrelation in the residuals from a regression analysis. A value of approximately 2 suggests no autocorrelation, values significantly less than 2 suggest positive autocorrelation, and values significantly greater than 2 suggest negative autocorrelation. Given a statistic of 1.53, which is below 2, the residuals appear to be positively autocorrelated.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
