    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The observation that mouse and human cell-surface proteins mix in the plasma membrane of a fused cell indicates that cell fusion was used, allowing the membranes to merge and proteins to diffuse within the shared membrane plane. This experimental setup is classically achieved using techniques that induce fusion of two different cells, such as polyethylene glycol (PEG) or viral fusogens. The most direct method described among the options is cell fusion.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
