    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "When three identical triangular prisms are joined by their rectangular faces, the equilateral triangular ends remain exposed on the two outer prisms, contributing 2 triangular faces. The rectangular faces merge along the sides: each pair of adjacent prisms shares a rectangular face, forming 3 large rectangular faces along the length and 2 outer ones, totaling 5 large rectangular faces. Additionally, the top and bottom each form one large face from three co-planar rectangles, adding 2 more, for a total of 2 (triangles) + 5 (sides) + 2 (top/bottom) = 9 faces.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
