    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the solution for the equationX=AX+bu;X(0) = X_0 where A=\\vert10\\vert,b=\\vert1\\vert,X_0 =\\vert- 1\\vert, \\vert- 22\\vert\\vert2\\vert\\vert0\\vert u(t) = \\delta(t) (impulse function).\n\nOptions: \nA. -3\nB. 2\nC. 0\nD. 3\nE. 10\nF. -2\nG. 22\nH. 1\nI. -10\nJ. -1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let’s break this down:  \n\nWe have  \n\\[\n\\dot{X} = AX + b u, \\quad X(0) = X_0 = \\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix},\n\\]\nwith  \n\\[\nA = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 \\end{bmatrix},\n\\quad b = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\end{bmatrix},\n\\quad u(t) = \\delta(t).\n\\]  \n\nThe impulse response adds a discontinuity in \\( X \\) at \\( t=0^{+} \\):  \n\\[\nX(0^{+}) = X_0 + b \\cdot 1 = \\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ 2 \\end{bmatrix}.\n\\]  \nThat means just after \\( t=0 \\), \\( X_1(0^{+}) = 0 \\), \\( X_2(0^{+}) = 2 \\).  \n\nThe homogeneous solution for \\( t>0 \\) is \\( X(t) = e^{At} X(0^{+}) \\).  \n\nThey likely ask for something like \\( X_1(t) \\) or \\( X_2(t) \\) at a certain \\( t \\) or maybe the final value for some component? But looking at options (small integers), maybe they simply want \\( X_1(0^{+}) \\) from the impulse effect.  \nFrom \\( X(0^{+}) = (0, 2)^T \\), \\( X_1(0^{+}) = 0 \\), which matches option **C. 0**.  \n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{C}\\)",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 186,
        "output_tokens": 357,
