      "generated_answer": "First, evaluate the system function $H(j\\omega) = \\frac{2j\\omega}{1+2j\\omega}$ at the input frequency $\\omega = 1$, which yields $H(j1) = \\frac{2j}{1+2j} = 0.8 + j0.4$. Next, calculate the time-domain response by taking the real part of the product of this complex gain and $e^{jt}$, resulting in $0.8\\cos t - 0.4\\sin t$. Finally, recognizing that $0.8 = 4/5$ and $0.4 = 2/5$, this result matches the expression in Option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
