    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the open-circuit emf (E) of the alternator, use the formula: \n\n\\[ E = 4.44 \\times f \\times \\Phi \\times T \\times K_p \\times K_d \\]\n\nwhere \\( f = 60 \\) Hz (frequency), \\( \\Phi = 0.025 \\) Wb (flux per pole), \\( T = \\frac{P \\times C}{A} = 6 \\times 4 = 24 \\) (total number of conductors per phase because armature coils are in series & phases are Y-connected), \\( K_p = \\frac{5}{6} \\) (pitch factor), and \\( K_d = 1 \\) (distribution factor since not given otherwise). \n\nCalculate: \n\n\\[ E = 4.44 \\times 60 \\times 0.025 \\times 24 \\times \\frac{5}{6} \\times 1 = 513 \\text{ Volts} \\]\n\nThus, the most likely correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).",
