      "generated_answer": "The study shows that mitochondrial dynamics change significantly during programmed cell death (PCD) in lace plant leaves, with distinct stages correlating with PCD progression. Inhibiting mitochondrial permeability transition pore (PTP) formation with cyclosporine A reduced PCD and perforation formation, indicating functional involvement. Therefore, mitochondria play a key role in leaf remodelling during PCD.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 463,
        "output_tokens": 85,
        "total_tokens": 548
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": 4.1373e-05,
    "accuracy": 1.0,
    "for_optimality": true
