    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nThe study introduces the hypothesis that alterations in creatine homeostasis occur during pregnancy to ensure sufficient substrate supply for maternal and fetal tissues. The results confirm significant physiological changes, including reduced plasma creatine and urinary excretion alongside increased tissue creatine content and transporter expression. These specific changes support the conclusion that the alteration is a metabolic adaptation necessary to maintain homeostasis during gestation.",
