    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{J}.  \nWilliam Lloyd Garrison argued that free Black people were entitled to full citizenship rights under the Constitution, a view directly contradicted by the Dred Scott v. Sanford (1857) decision, in which the Supreme Court ruled that African Americans, whether free or enslaved, could not be U.S. citizens. This decision denied Black people constitutional rights and reinforced racial distinctions, opposing Garrison’s belief in their equal legal standing.",
      "success": true,
