      "generated_answer": "The Sugar Act imposed taxes on imported goods to raise revenue and regulate trade to protect British interests in the colonies. Protective tariffs established during the Industrial Revolution similarly used taxes on imports to increase government funds and secure economic interests. Both policies relied on the regulation and taxation of commerce rather than direct taxation or monetary policy.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
