      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nMao Zedong's text advocates for the collectivization of agriculture to eliminate capitalism and solidify a worker-peasant alliance, which mirrors the Soviet Union's policies of forced agricultural collectivization under Joseph Stalin. This approach was designed to transform individual production into a socialist structure, distinguishing it from Western ideologies like capitalism, liberalism, or social democracy. Consequently, Stalin's communist principles represent the primary ideological influence behind Mao's policy proposals in this passage.",
