      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}.\n\nVoltaire's work critiques religious intolerance and blind optimism (theodicy), reflecting the Enlightenment's push for reason and skepticism about religious dogma. David Hume was a contemporary philosopher who similarly challenged religious authority and metaphysical certainty through empiricism and skepticism. Therefore, their philosophical critiques of unfounded authority and optimistic dogma are most closely aligned.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
